<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gencor lifts half year shr, div up.</title>
<headline>Gencor lifts half year shr, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-excepts (cts)	  60.2 vs   40.5</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)		111.2 vs   48.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			    8.5 vs    7.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		    1,879 vs    702</p>
<p>    Attrib income (pre-except)   1,018 vs    586</p>
<p>    Net operating income	   1,609 vs  1,177</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 401 vs    214</p>
<p>    Investment income		  447 vs    379</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			    2,336 vs  1,150</p>
<p>    Tax				    350 vs    291</p>
<p>    Net finance charges		168 vs    250</p>
<p>    Outside shareholders' interest 140 vs    230</p>
<p>    Net exceptional gain	     861 vs    116</p>
<p>    Net investment income	    447 vs    379</p>
<p>    Turnover			   9,377 vs  6,543</p>
<p>    Explorations/project costs     180 vs     97</p>
<p>Attrib income by commodity:</p>
<p>    - Aluminium			  381 vs    218</p>
<p>    - Steel and Ferroalloys	  104 vs    204</p>
<p>    - Titanium Minerals		210 vs     99</p>
<p>    - Coal				 145 vs     55</p>
<p>    - Wits Gold			   69 vs     33</p>
<p>    - Base metals			 36 vs     26</p>
<p>    - International gold		21 vs     35</p>
<p>    - Platinum			    23 vs	9</p>
<p>    - TOTAL				989 vs    679</p>
<p>Attrib income by country:</p>
<p>    - South Africa		     745 vs    393</p>
<p>    - Brazil			     114 vs    117</p>
<p>    - Suriname			    55 vs     54</p>
<p>    - Canada				17 vs     22</p>
<p>    - Indonesia			   16 vs     32</p>
<p>    - Australia			   18 vs     15</p>
<p>    - Colombia			    24 vs     46</p>
<p>    - TOTAL				989 VS    679</p>
<p>Div payable March 27</p>
<p>On register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Gencor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters predicted a consensus EPS pre-exceptionals of 64.1 cents with the range 60-69 and a dividend of 9.0 cents with the range 8-10.</p>
<p>The company said exceptional items reflected capital gains on the realisation of long-term investments and capital gains in group operations.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
